WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.170
If every group uses up some of a limited supply,

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.970
the supply limits how many groups you can have.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.330
Twelve tokens, three per group,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.990
means at most four groups.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.630
You know that before making a single group.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.640
This gives the first half of a "largest possible"

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.290
answer: a ceiling.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.020
The second half is showing that the ceiling can

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.070
actually be reached.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.230
A complete solution needs both.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.690
Five students are in a club.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.350
Each day, two pairs work together and one student rests.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.510
No two students may be partners more than once.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.830
What is the largest number of days this can continue?

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.670
Pause and decide what is being used up.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.200
The supply is pairs of students.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.820
Five students form ten different pairs.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.160
Each day uses two new pairs.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.360
So there can be at most five days.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.110
Can five days really be done?

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.170
Here is a schedule.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.390
Day one: A with B, C with D.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.410
Day two: A with C, B with E.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.570
Day three: A with D, C with E.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.330
Day four: A with E, B with D.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.130
Day five: B with C, D with E.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.750
All ten pairs appear exactly once.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.840
What if each group has three people?

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.640
Counting pairs gives a ceiling of three groups.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.740
But any two legal groups must share exactly one person.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:26.480
Two triples cannot be disjoint among five people,

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.660
and sharing two would repeat a pair.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.110
For a third group, using the shared person repeats a

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.560
pair with any other person.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.490
Leaving that person out forces three choices from the

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.060
two outer pairs, so one pair repeats.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.980
Two groups fit, and a third never does.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.200
Find the limited supply.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:45.900
Divide to get a ceiling.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.540
Then either build an example that reaches it,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.540
or explain why it cannot be reached.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.760
Notebook challenge: six students play chess,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.580
one game per pair at most.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.820
Each day three games are played.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.480
What is the largest possible number of days?
